After seeing the posting recommending some of the less popular character
classes, I thought I'd try a few games as an archeologist.  If you
haven't tried this character, I recommend it.  They start off typically
with low strength and dexterity (8! in my current game).  But there are
advantages:

- Start off fast, with pickaxe and tinning kit.  This lets you run away
and throw things.  (I carried around tons of poison arrows, which let me
kill almost anything from a distance.)  You can also dig pits and
trapdoors to injure or detour particular monsters.  The tinning kit lets
you get lots of intrinsics without corpses going bad, and lets you leave
caches of food that are handy when you double back late in the game.
Tins are much lighter than the actual monsters and don't take as long to
eat.

- Archeologists start off with all gems identified -- you don't waste
energy carring around pieces of glass, and unicorns give you all that
nice extra luck.  I found my first dilithium crystal (on the castle
level), they do exist!

- For some reason, my hit points are going up very slowly.  I've cleared
out the castle level and only have 81 hp.  I've found that with a camera
and ring of conflict, you should be invincible.  The camera lets you
blind nymphs, liches, and similar nasties.  This is the first game I
ever enchanted gauntlets of dexterity -- hey, I though the enchantment
_only_ applied to dexterity, but you get the AC bonus too!  Still, with
a dexterity of 12, unenchanted Demonbane, and 81 hp this must be one of
the weakest characters to ever make it to the castle.

- Found out the hard way what happens when you piss off your god.  You
lose all the AC bonus granted by priest(esse)s!  I lost about 3 AC after
praying too often, then another 2 after I ate a wraith corpse to go up a
level (bug?).

- The hand of Elbereth happened while I was wielding Demonbane, and
afterwards I found it rustproofed.  Handy against black puddings (as is
the ring of conflict).  I thought I'd somehow get Excalibur though?  I
don't detect any better damage bonus on Demonbane now that I'm the hand.
I guess I'll keep using it now that it's +5, it's been handy against
*cubi and minor demons, so I'm not too worried about balrogs.

John

